<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!-- The generator set's upgrades (docs/development/vehicle-generator-set.md). Figures and costs authored. Node keys are saved in the game: never rename or remove one. Not yet tested in game. -->
  <Vehicles.UpgradeTreeDef>
    <defName>Phobos_GeneratorSet_UpgradeTree</defName>
    <modExtensions>
      <!-- Priced like our fittings and tunes (Framework 0.106.0; owner, 13 Nov 2026): the figures below are the base. -->
      <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosUpgradeCostsLikeTunes" />
    </modExtensions>
    <nodes>
    <li>
      <key>BiggerAlternator</key>
      <label>Uprated alternator</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A bigger alternator behind the cab: 650 W more at full output, and fuel burned at the same watts per unit.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/Upgrades/BiggerAlternator</icon>
      <work>3000</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(2, 2)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>Electricity</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_GeneratorOutput</def>
              <!-- 650 W since Vehicles 0.51.0, in proportion to the 2,000 W set (was 400 on 1,200; authored). -->
              <value>650</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
      </upgrades>
      <ingredients>
        <!-- Beside one alternator, which the vehicle's parts bill adds (Bill_GeneratorSet.xml). -->
        <Steel>50</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
      <graphicOverlays>
        <li>
          <graphicData>
            <texPath>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/GeneratorSet_BiggerGenerator</texPath>
            <graphicClass>Vehicles.Graphic_Vehicle</graphicClass>
            <drawSize>(4, 9)</drawSize>
            <shaderType>Cutout</shaderType>
            <layer>1</layer>
          </graphicData>
        </li>
      </graphicOverlays>
    </li>
    <li>
      <key>CableReel</key>
      <label>Cable reel</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A long cable on a drum. You choose where the cable end goes, up to 12 cells from the truck, so the truck can stand somewhere safe.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/Upgrades/CableReel</icon>
      <work>1500</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(7, 2)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>Electricity</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_CableReach</def>
              <value>12</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
      </upgrades>
      <ingredients>
        <Steel>40</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>1</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
      <graphicOverlays>
        <li>
          <graphicData>
            <texPath>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/GeneratorSet_Reel</texPath>
            <graphicClass>Vehicles.Graphic_Vehicle</graphicClass>
            <drawSize>(4, 9)</drawSize>
            <shaderType>Cutout</shaderType>
            <layer>1</layer>
          </graphicData>
        </li>
      </graphicOverlays>
    </li>
    <li>
      <key>BatteryBuffer</key>
      <label>Battery buffer</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A battery box under the deck. It fills from spare power and keeps the grid alive for a time when the tank runs dry or the engine is hurt.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/Upgrades/BatteryBuffer</icon>
      <work>2000</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(12, 2)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>Batteries</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_GeneratorBuffer</def>
              <value>150</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
      </upgrades>
      <ingredients>
        <!-- Beside two batteries, which the vehicle's parts bill adds (Bill_GeneratorSet.xml): the buffer's own electronics. -->
        <ComponentIndustrial>6</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
      <graphicOverlays>
        <li>
          <graphicData>
            <texPath>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/GeneratorSet_Battery</texPath>
            <graphicClass>Vehicles.Graphic_Vehicle</graphicClass>
            <drawSize>(4, 9)</drawSize>
            <shaderType>Cutout</shaderType>
            <layer>1</layer>
          </graphicData>
        </li>
      </graphicOverlays>
    </li>
    <li>
      <!-- Vehicles 0.100.0 (owner, 22 Nov 2026: the jamming truck on the Busbar; docs/development/ea6b-prowler.md, step 4). A mast of antennas
           that jams within 18 cells while the set is set up and running, taking 800 W off the top of its output (the rules Def's figures,
           authored; D'thorga Framework's CompPhobosGeneratorSet and JamFields). Inside the field, other factions' vehicles lose their radar and
           warning receiver. Its icon and overlay are the owner's pick of 25 Nov 2026 (paid, try 2), the mast folded across the rear deck and
           the icon cut from the same picture (assets/phobos-vehicles/export_paid25_parts.py; Vehicles 0.117.3). Since Vehicles 0.130.1
           (Framework 0.355.0; docs/development/electronic-warfare.md, EW11) it has a switch: radar, radios (with the Radio Framework), both,
           or off. -->
      <key>GroundJammer</key>
      <label>Jammer mast</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A folding mast of jamming antennas, powered from the generator, with a switch for what it jams. While the set is set up and running, it floods the air with noise: switched to radar, for 18 cells around, enemy aircraft and vehicles inside lose their radar and their warning of attack; switched to radios, every radio for a long way around is drowned, the colony's own as well. It takes 800 W of the set's output while it jams, so less reaches the grid.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/Upgrades/JammerMast</icon>
      <work>4000</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(17, 2)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>MicroelectronicsBasics</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <ingredients>
        <Steel>60</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>6</ComponentIndustrial>
        <ComponentSpacer>2</ComponentSpacer>
      </ingredients>
      <graphicOverlays>
        <li>
          <graphicData>
            <texPath>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/GeneratorSet_JammerMast</texPath>
            <graphicClass>Vehicles.Graphic_Vehicle</graphicClass>
            <drawSize>(4, 9)</drawSize>
            <shaderType>Cutout</shaderType>
            <layer>1</layer>
          </graphicData>
        </li>
      </graphicOverlays>
    </li>
    <li>
      <!-- Owner, 11 Nov 2026 (docs/development/vehicle-upgrades-round-two.md, the generator set's signature). The share and the output
           cost are authored; the heat rate and the 21 C target come from the game's own heater (CompPhobosGeneratorSet). Its icon and
           overlay are the owner's pick of 12 Nov 2026. -->
      <key>HeatRecovery</key>
      <label>Exhaust heat exchanger</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A heat exchanger on the exhaust. While the set makes power, it warms the room the cable end stands in, more as more power is drawn, until the room reaches 21 C. Outdoors the heat goes to waste. The exchanger's back pressure costs 25 W of output.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/Upgrades/HeatExchanger</icon>
      <work>1500</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(7, 7)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>Electricity</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_HeatRecovery</def>
              <value>0.6</value>
            </li>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_GeneratorOutput</def>
              <value>-25</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
      </upgrades>
      <ingredients>
        <Steel>40</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
      <graphicOverlays>
        <li>
          <graphicData>
            <texPath>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/GeneratorSet_HeatExchanger</texPath>
            <graphicClass>Vehicles.Graphic_Vehicle</graphicClass>
            <drawSize>(4, 9)</drawSize>
            <shaderType>Cutout</shaderType>
            <layer>1</layer>
          </graphicData>
        </li>
      </graphicOverlays>
    </li>
    <li>
      <!-- Owner, 12 Nov 2026: the heavy-duty fan, fan picture 2 as the upgrade of the stock fan. What it is for (agent proposal, owner to
           revise; docs/development/vehicle-generator-set.md): a parked radiator cools at 0.7 of its moving rate, and the fan's 0.3 brings
           it to the full rate, so a set left working hard in summer heat keeps its coolant in hand. Cost authored. -->
      <key>HeavyFan</key>
      <label>Heavy-duty fan</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A bigger cooling fan with a heavier guard. A parked engine's radiator gets no air from driving; this fan moves as much air through it as the road would, so the set stays cool working hard in hot weather.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/Vehicles/GeneratorSet/Upgrades/HeavyFan</icon>
      <work>1200</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(12, 7)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>Electricity</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_StoppedAirflow</def>
              <value>0.3</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
      </upgrades>
      <ingredients>
        <Steel>30</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>1</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
    </li>
    <li>
      <!-- D'thorga Vehicles 0.135.0 (the owner's word of 28 Nov 2026: "Perhaps we add a turbo generator to our Busbar? As an upgrade, of course").
           Electric turbo-compounding: a power turbine in the exhaust turns a high-speed generator, winning electricity back from heat that
           would leave by the stack, with no more fuel. Sold for diesel generator sets (Bowman Power's electric turbo compounding units, from
           memory, unverified), which claim some 5 to 10 % more output; 150 W on the 2,000 W set is 7.5 % (authored). Its watts are counted as
           recovered (Phobos_RecoveredWatts), so they burn no chemfuel (D'thorga Framework 0.377.0). It sits inside the exhaust, so nothing is
           drawn on the truck; its icon is the turbocharger fitting's until the night run draws its own. It goes beside the heat exchanger:
           both take from the same exhaust, which here is a simplification (the exchanger's heat is not lowered by the turbine). -->
      <key>PhobosExhaustTurboGenerator</key>
      <label>Exhaust turbo-generator</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A small turbine in the exhaust that turns a fast generator, winning electricity back from heat that would go out the stack. The set makes 150 W more at full output, for no more fuel.</description>
      <upgradeExplanation>Output: 150 W more at full output, burning no fuel of its own.\nAt part load it gives its share, as the exhaust's heat falls with the load.</upgradeExplanation>
      <icon>Phobos/VehicleSystems/Fittings/Turbocharger</icon>
      <work>2500</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(17, 7)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>PhobosResearch_Turbines</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_GeneratorOutput</def>
              <value>150</value>
            </li>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_RecoveredWatts</def>
              <value>150</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
      </upgrades>
      <ingredients>
        <!-- The turbine, the high-speed generator and its power electronics (authored). -->
        <Steel>40</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>4</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
    </li>
    <li>
      <!-- Owner, 12 Nov 2026: the service lead, batch 3 signature (docs/development/vehicle-upgrades-round-two.md). Reach and cost authored;
           the lead's 300 W is in the rules Def. No picture on the body: the lead is drawn as a line while the set is selected. -->
      <key>PhobosServiceLead</key>
      <label>Service lead</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>A heavy cable on a small reel, with clamps and a charger. While the set is set up and running, the lead reaches one of your vehicles within 6 cells, charges its battery, and gives it a start if it is too flat to start. It takes 300 W before the camp's grid does.</description>
      <icon>Phobos/VehicleSystems/ServiceLead</icon>
      <work>1200</work>
      <gridCoordinate>(2, 7)</gridCoordinate>
      <drawSize>(80, 80)</drawSize>
      <researchPrerequisites>
        <li>Electricity</li>
      </researchPrerequisites>
      <upgrades>
        <li Class="Vehicles.StatUpgrade">
          <vehicleStats>
            <li>
              <def>Phobos_ServiceLeadReach</def>
              <value>6</value>
            </li>
          </vehicleStats>
        </li>
      </upgrades>
      <ingredients>
        <Steel>30</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
    </li>
    <li>
      <!-- Armour kits without a picture of their own (D'thorga Vehicles 0.80.0; vehicle-militarised-service-vehicles.md, "The kits").
           Each raises named parts by class with Add (vehicle-armour.md; Combat Extended's figures in Mods/CombatExtended), and its real
           kilograms [A] load the engine as cargo would (owner, 19 Nov 2026), taking cargo room on the Talus only. Figures and costs authored.
           scripts/check-vehicle-armour.py holds each kit to its class on both scales. Not yet tested in game. -->
      <key>PhobosEngineGuards</key>
      <label>Engine and tank guards</label>
      <displayLabel>true</displayLabel>
      <description>Steel guards around the engine and the fuel tank, against rifle fire. A guarded tank still leaks and a guarded engine still burns once they are finally holed: it takes heavier fire to get there.</description>
      <upgradeExplanation>Engine and fuel tank: from skin to rifle armour, which stops ordinary rifle bullets.\nKit weight: 300 kg more, carried as cargo.</upgradeExplanation>
      <icon>Phobos/Vehicles/Upgrades/EngineGuards</icon>
